----------------------------------------------------------------------
DEVIATIONS FROM UPSTREAM
----------------------------------------------------------------------

The following describe how this fork differs from upstream. They are
behavioral facts about the code in this tree, not marketing.

- Product and binary rebranded to "Hanzo Dev": the CLI ships as the `dev`
  binary (codex-rs/cli/Cargo.toml `name = "dev"`; codex-rs/cli/src/main.rs
  banner `/// Hanzo Dev`), distributed as the npm package `@hanzo/dev`
  ("Hanzo AI coding assistant"); the workspace root is `hanzo-dev-monorepo`.

- Default model provider is the Hanzo LLM gateway: `HANZO_PROVIDER_ID = "hanzo"`
  targeting `https://api.hanzo.ai/v1` (OpenAI-compatible, Responses wire API).
  When no provider is configured, config resolution falls back to `hanzo`
  (codex-rs/core/src/config/mod.rs; codex-rs/model-provider-info/src/lib.rs).

- Added a `Hanzo` authentication mode backed by Hanzo IAM (hanzo.id OAuth):
  public client `HANZO_CLIENT_ID = "hanzo-app"`, credentials from
  `HANZO_API_KEY` / `HANZO_USER_KEY` (codex-rs/login/src/auth/manager.rs,
  codex-rs/cli/src/login.rs), alongside the existing ApiKey and ChatGPT modes.

- Added Hanzo local/self-hosted provider defaults: `HANZO_LOCAL_BASE_URL`
  (http://localhost:1234/v1) and `HANZO_NODE_BASE_URL` (http://localhost:36900/v1),
  the latter overridable via `HANZO_NODE_URL` (codex-rs/model-provider-info/src/lib.rs).

- OpenAI and ChatGPT remain first-class, selectable providers (OPENAI_API_KEY,
  "Sign in with ChatGPT", `https://api.openai.com/v1`); nothing OpenAI-specific
  was disabled — Hanzo is added as the default, not a replacement.

- Consolidated to a single Rust workspace (codex-rs) that builds the `dev`
  binary; parallel legacy trees were removed (see CLAUDE.md changelog).

- Added Hanzo-specific subtrees not present upstream: `hanzo-node/` and
  `dev-cli/` npm distribution, `hanzo-cli/`, `platform/`, `deploy/`, `sdk/`,
  `contracts/`, and `oss-payments/`.

- On systems where `code` is already taken (e.g. VS Code) the CLI is also
  installed as `coder` (codex-cli/bin/coder.js).

- Upstream tracking is automated via `.github/workflows/upstream-sync.yml`,
  which merges `openai/codex@main` into a draft PR (never auto-merged).

